{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install the package with pnpm:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm add @tanstack/markdown","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"html-and-parser-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"HTML and parser usage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The parser and HTML renderer have no peer dependencies:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { renderHtml } from '@tanstack/markdown/html'\n\nconst html = renderHtml('# Hello')","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the narrowest entry point your application needs:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { parseMarkdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/parser'\nimport { renderHtml } from '@tanstack/markdown/html'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/markdown"},{"type":"text","value":" entry re-exports the parser, HTML renderer, inline parser, and all public types."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"react-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React usage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The React adapter requires React 18 or newer:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm add @tanstack/markdown react","lang":"bash"},{"type":"code","value":"import { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\n\nexport function Article({ source }: { source: string }) {\n  return <Markdown>{source}</Markdown>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React is a peer dependency and is not bundled into the adapter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"octane-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Octane usage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Octane adapter requires Octane 0.1.12 or newer:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm add @tanstack/markdown octane","lang":"bash"},{"type":"code","value":"import { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/octane'\n\nexport function Article({ source }: { source: string }) @{\n  <Markdown>{source}</Markdown>\n}","lang":"tsrx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Octane is an optional peer dependency and is not bundled into the adapter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"runtime-and-module-format","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime and module format"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Markdown ships ESM JavaScript and TypeScript declarations. Its synchronous core works in modern browsers, server runtimes, build tools, React server rendering, and Octane server rendering."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"optional-capabilities","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional capabilities"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Syntax highlighting is supplied as a callback, so install only the highlighter your application uses. Docs-specific behavior is available through separately importable "},{"type":"link","href":"./guides/extensions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extensions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":1},{"id":"html-and-parser-usage","text":"HTML and parser usage","level":2},{"id":"react-usage","text":"React usage","level":2},{"id":"octane-usage","text":"Octane usage","level":2},{"id":"runtime-and-module-format","text":"Runtime and module format","level":2},{"id":"optional-capabilities","text":"Optional capabilities","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Installation\n\nInstall the package with pnpm:\n\n```bash\npnpm add @tanstack/markdown\n```\n\n## HTML and parser usage\n\nThe parser and HTML renderer have no peer dependencies:\n\n```ts\nimport { renderHtml } from '@tanstack/markdown/html'\n\nconst html = renderHtml('# Hello')\n```\n\nUse the narrowest entry point your application needs:\n\n```ts\nimport { parseMarkdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/parser'\nimport { renderHtml } from '@tanstack/markdown/html'\n```\n\nThe default `@tanstack/markdown` entry re-exports the parser, HTML renderer, inline parser, and all public types.\n\n## React usage\n\nThe React adapter requires React 18 or newer:\n\n```bash\npnpm add @tanstack/markdown react\n```\n\n```tsx\nimport { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\n\nexport function Article({ source }: { source: string }) {\n  return <Markdown>{source}</Markdown>\n}\n```\n\nReact is a peer dependency and is not bundled into the adapter.\n\n## Octane usage\n\nThe Octane adapter requires Octane 0.1.12 or newer:\n\n```bash\npnpm add @tanstack/markdown octane\n```\n\n```tsrx\nimport { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/octane'\n\nexport function Article({ source }: { source: string }) @{\n  <Markdown>{source}</Markdown>\n}\n```\n\nOctane is an optional peer dependency and is not bundled into the adapter.\n\n## Runtime and module format\n\nTanStack Markdown ships ESM JavaScript and TypeScript declarations. Its synchronous core works in modern browsers, server runtimes, build tools, React server rendering, and Octane server rendering.\n\n## Optional capabilities\n\nSyntax highlighting is supplied as a callback, so install only the highlighter your application uses. Docs-specific behavior is available through separately importable [extensions](./guides/extensions.md).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Installation\n---\n\n# Installation\n\nInstall the package with pnpm:\n\n```bash\npnpm add @tanstack/markdown\n```\n\n## HTML and parser usage\n\nThe parser and HTML renderer have no peer dependencies:\n\n```ts\nimport { renderHtml } from '@tanstack/markdown/html'\n\nconst html = renderHtml('# Hello')\n```\n\nUse the narrowest entry point your application needs:\n\n```ts\nimport { parseMarkdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/parser'\nimport { renderHtml } from '@tanstack/markdown/html'\n```\n\nThe default `@tanstack/markdown` entry re-exports the parser, HTML renderer, inline parser, and all public types.\n\n## React usage\n\nThe React adapter requires React 18 or newer:\n\n```bash\npnpm add @tanstack/markdown react\n```\n\n```tsx\nimport { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\n\nexport function Article({ source }: { source: string }) {\n  return <Markdown>{source}</Markdown>\n}\n```\n\nReact is a peer dependency and is not bundled into the adapter.\n\n## Octane usage\n\nThe Octane adapter requires Octane 0.1.12 or newer:\n\n```bash\npnpm add @tanstack/markdown octane\n```\n\n```tsrx\nimport { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/octane'\n\nexport function Article({ source }: { source: string }) @{\n  <Markdown>{source}</Markdown>\n}\n```\n\nOctane is an optional peer dependency and is not bundled into the adapter.\n\n## Runtime and module format\n\nTanStack Markdown ships ESM JavaScript and TypeScript declarations. Its synchronous core works in modern browsers, server runtimes, build tools, React server rendering, and Octane server rendering.\n\n## Optional capabilities\n\nSyntax highlighting is supplied as a callback, so install only the highlighter your application uses. Docs-specific behavior is available through separately importable [extensions](./guides/extensions.md).\n"}
